IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `psga-directions`
IMPORT `psga-finance`

-- Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, Part 5 and ss 42, 45 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures -- bodies`

GIVEN `is established by a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Town Council` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `schedule listing` IS A ScheduleListing,
      `main function is regulating a profession` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `main function is representing the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BodyFacts
DECIDE `a body of the kind` `is established by a public Act` `is a Town Council` `schedule listing` `main function is regulating a profession` `main function is representing the community` IS
    BodyFacts WITH
        `a body corporate established by a public Act for the purposes of a public function` IS `is established by a public Act`
        `a Town Council established under section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988` IS `is a Town Council`
        `listed in` IS `schedule listing`
        `its main function is to regulate the practice and standards of a profession` IS `main function is regulating a profession`
        `its main function is to represent particular community interests or the volunteer movement` IS `main function is representing the community`

`a Group 1A board` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`DSTA, the only Group 1B body` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`the People's Association, the only Group 1C body` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 3 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a Group 2A regulator` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Second Schedule` TRUE FALSE
`a Group 2B regulator` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the Second Schedule` TRUE FALSE
`a Part 1 Second Schedule body that does not regulate a profession` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Second Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a Group 3A community body` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE
`a Group 3B community body` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE
`a public body in no Schedule` MEANS `a body of the kind` TRUE FALSE `no Schedule` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 33 -- who Part 5 applies to`

#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Group 1A board`
#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `DSTA, the only Group 1B body`
#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `the People's Association, the only Group 1C body`
#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Group 2A regulator`
#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Group 2B regulator`
#ASSERT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Group 3B community body`

-- GROUP 3A IS NOT NAMED, and a Part 1 Second Schedule body failing the main-function test is not Group 2.
#ASSERT NOT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Group 3A community body`
#ASSERT NOT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a Part 1 Second Schedule body that does not regulate a profession`
#ASSERT NOT `Part 5 applies to the body` `a public body in no Schedule`

-- THE GROUP 1B CARVE-OUT. The audit and Parliament provisions apply to everyone Part 5 reaches except
-- Group 1B, which is the Defence Science and Technology Agency alone.
#ASSERT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `a Group 1A board`
#ASSERT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `the People's Association, the only Group 1C body`
#ASSERT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `a Group 2A regulator`
#ASSERT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `a Group 3B community body`
#ASSERT NOT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `DSTA, the only Group 1B body`
#ASSERT NOT `the audit and Parliament provisions apply to the body` `a Group 3A community body`

#ASSERT `the constitutional Act's requirement prevails over Part 5` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the constitutional Act's requirement prevails over Part 5` FALSE

§ `Sections 34 and 35 -- estimates`

GIVEN `prepared and adopted` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the following year` IS A BOOLEAN, `sent to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Estimates
DECIDE `estimates of the kind` `prepared and adopted` `for the following year` `sent to the Minister` IS
    Estimates WITH
        `the estimates were prepared and adopted during the financial year` IS `prepared and adopted`
        `they cover the following financial year` IS `for the following year`
        `a copy was sent to the responsible Minister as soon as possible after adoption` IS `sent to the Minister`

#ASSERT `the annual estimates duty in section 34 is met` (`estimates of the kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the annual estimates duty in section 34 is met` (`estimates of the kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- The estimates are for the FOLLOWING year, not the current one.
#ASSERT NOT `the annual estimates duty in section 34 is met` (`estimates of the kind` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the annual estimates duty in section 34 is met` (`estimates of the kind` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- s 35: supplementary estimates are a permission.
#ASSERT NOT `a public body must prepare supplementary estimates`

§ `Section 36 -- accounts and records`

GIVEN `records kept` IS A BOOLEAN, `payments authorised` IS A BOOLEAN, `assets controlled` IS A BOOLEAN, `expenditure controlled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Controls
DECIDE `controls of the kind` `records kept` `payments authorised` `assets controlled` `expenditure controlled` IS
    Controls WITH
        `proper accounts and records are kept in accordance with written law` IS `records kept`
        `all payments out of its moneys are correctly made and properly authorised` IS `payments authorised`
        `adequate control is maintained over property and assets` IS `assets controlled`
        `adequate control is maintained over expenditure` IS `expenditure controlled`

#ASSERT `the duties in section 36 are met` (`controls of the kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duties in section 36 are met` (`controls of the kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duties in section 36 are met` (`controls of the kind` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duties in section 36 are met` (`controls of the kind` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duties in section 36 are met` (`controls of the kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Section 37 -- the auditor`

GIVEN `the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `appointed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `appointed annually` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in consultation with the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a registered public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AuditorAppointment
DECIDE `an auditor appointment` `the Auditor-General` `appointed by the Minister` `appointed annually` `in consultation with the Auditor-General` `a registered public accountant` IS
    AuditorAppointment WITH
        `the auditor is the Auditor-General` IS `the Auditor-General`
        `appointed by the responsible Minister` IS `appointed by the Minister`
        `appointed for the year, annually` IS `appointed annually`
        `in consultation with the Auditor-General` IS `in consultation with the Auditor-General`
        `a public accountant registered or deemed registered under the Accountants Act 2004` IS `a registered public accountant`

#ASSERT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- The Minister appoints, annually, in consultation, and the appointee is a registered public accountant.
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- Appointed by the public body itself, not the Minister.
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor is validly appointed under section 37` (`an auditor appointment` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `the auditor's remuneration is paid out of the funds of the public body` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor's remuneration is paid out of the funds of the public body` TRUE

§ `Section 38 -- the auditor's powers, and the offence`

GIVEN `a requirement was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise hindered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN ObstructionFacts
DECIDE `an obstruction` `a requirement was made` `failed to comply` `had reasonable cause` `otherwise hindered` IS
    ObstructionFacts WITH
        `the auditor or an authorised person made a requirement under section 38(2)` IS `a requirement was made`
        `the person failed to comply with it` IS `failed to comply`
        `the person had reasonable cause` IS `had reasonable cause`
        `the person otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor in performing functions or exercising powers` IS `otherwise hindered`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Limb (a) has the reasonable-cause escape.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Limb (b) has none.
#ASSERT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- No requirement, no failure.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 38(3) is committed` (`an obstruction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- A fine only, at a fifth of the s 7 level.
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 38(3), in dollars` EQUALS 1000

§ `Section 39 -- the auditor's report`

GIVEN `fairly` IS A BOOLEAN, `records` IS A BOOLEAN, `in accordance` IS A BOOLEAN, `other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ReportContent
DECIDE `report content` `fairly` `records` `in accordance` `other matters` IS
    ReportContent WITH
        `says whether the statements show fairly the transactions and state of affairs` IS `fairly`
        `says whether proper accounting and other records were kept, including records of all assets` IS `records`
        `says whether receipts, expenditure, investments and dealings in assets were in accordance with the Act, the constitutional Act and other written law` IS `in accordance`
        `reports any other matter arising from the audit that the auditor considers should be reported` IS `other matters`

#ASSERT `the report states what section 39(1) requires` (`report content` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the report states what section 39(1) requires` (`report content` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report states what section 39(1) requires` (`report content` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report states what section 39(1) requires` (`report content` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the report states what section 39(1) requires` (`report content` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- Even the auditor's direct line to the Minister runs through the body being audited.
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor may report to the Minister without passing the report through the public body`

§ `Sections 40 and 41 -- to the Minister and to Parliament`

GIVEN `sent to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed by the chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with the auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Auditor-General audited` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `forwarded to the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Reporting
DECIDE `a reporting` `sent to the Minister` `signed by the chairperson` `with the auditor's report` `the Auditor-General audited` `forwarded to the Auditor-General` IS
    Reporting WITH
        `the audited statements were sent to the responsible Minister` IS `sent to the Minister`
        `signed by the chairperson` IS `signed by the chairperson`
        `with the auditor's report under section 39(1)` IS `with the auditor's report`
        `the auditor is the Auditor-General` IS `the Auditor-General audited`
        `a non-Auditor-General auditor forwarded a copy to the Auditor-General at the same time as submitting to the public body` IS `forwarded to the Auditor-General`

#ASSERT `the audited statements were sent as section 40(1) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the audited statements were sent as section 40(1) requires` (`a reporting` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Signed by the chairperson, not the chief executive; and with the auditor's report.
#ASSERT NOT `the audited statements were sent as section 40(1) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the audited statements were sent as section 40(1) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 40(2): a copy to the Auditor-General, unless the Auditor-General is the auditor.
#ASSERT `the Auditor-General has been given a copy as section 40(2) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Auditor-General has been given a copy as section 40(2) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Auditor-General has been given a copy as section 40(2) requires` (`a reporting` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- ss 40(3), 41(2): presentation to Parliament, for everyone but Group 1B, with no deadline.
#ASSERT `the Minister must present the audited statements to Parliament` `a Group 1A board`
#ASSERT `the Minister must present the annual report to Parliament` `a Group 3B community body`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must present the audited statements to Parliament` `DSTA, the only Group 1B body`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must present the annual report to Parliament` `DSTA, the only Group 1B body`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act sets a deadline for presenting to Parliament`

§ `Section 42 -- amending the Schedules`

#ASSERT `section 42 authorises the order` `adds a body` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 42 authorises the order` `deletes a body` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 42 authorises the order` `replaces a body` FALSE

-- The one named exception: the Monetary Authority of Singapore may not be added.
#ASSERT NOT `section 42 authorises the order` `adds a body` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 42 authorises the order` `replaces a body` TRUE

-- Deleting is never a problem.
#ASSERT `section 42 authorises the order` `deletes a body` TRUE

§ `Section 45 -- saving and transitional`

#ASSERT `the direction continues in force as if given under section 5` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the direction continues in force as if given under section 5` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the direction continues in force as if given under section 5` TRUE FALSE

-- An old direction to a Group 2 or Group 3 body is treated as a s 5 direction although s 5 cannot reach that body.
#ASSERT `a saved pre-2018 direction is to a body a section 5 direction can reach` `a Group 1A board` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a saved pre-2018 direction is to a body a section 5 direction can reach` `a Group 2A regulator` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a saved pre-2018 direction is to a body a section 5 direction can reach` `a Group 3B community body` TRUE
